WHAT THIS COVERS

The browser port in unreal2/, the earlier standalone glenz-vectors port in
glenz-web/, the tools under both, and the site served from the repository
root are released into the public domain under the terms above. Take them,
fork them, ship them, sell them — no attribution required.

The original 1993 Second Reality source, data and executables that this
repository also contains were released into the public domain by Future Crew
themselves for the demo's 20th anniversary in 2013, under this same Unlicense.
See docs/README-futurecrew.md for their own statement.

So the entire repository is public domain, top to bottom. The only things NOT
covered are third-party components that carry their own (also permissive)
licences:

  unreal2/vendor/libopenmpt*     libopenmpt, BSD-2-Clause
  unreal2/vendor/chiptune3*      chiptune2/3.js, MIT
  glenz-web/vendor/libopenmpt*   libopenmpt, BSD-2-Clause
  glenz-web/vendor/chiptune3*    chiptune2/3.js, MIT
  glenz-web/vendor/three*        three.js, MIT

and, on the site pages only, the photographs of people, which remain the
property of their respective copyright holders and are used with attribution
recorded next to each image.
